  "result": "Safety Data Sheet (https://www.bio.vu.nl/~microb/Protocols/chemicals/MSDS/polyhydroxybutyric%20acid.pdf)\nciteturn16search12 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; - Product name: Poly[(R)-3-hydroxybutyric acid]\n- Product Number: 363502\nSIGMA-ALDRICH  \nsigma-aldrich.com\n\n# SAFETY DATA SHEET\naccording to Regulation (EC) No. 1907/2006  \nVersion 5.0 Revision Date 26.03.2013  \nPrint Date 21.08.2015  \nGENERIC EU MSDS - NO COUNTRY SPECIFIC DATA - NO OEL DATA\n\n## SECTION 1: Identification of the substance/mixture and of the company/undertaking\n\n### 1.1 Product identifiers\n- Product name: Poly[(R)-3-hydroxybutyric acid]\n- Product Number: 363502\n- Brand: Aldrich\n- REACH No.: A registration number is not available for this substance as the substance or its uses are exempted from registration, the annual tonnage does not require a registration or the registration is envisaged for a later registration deadline.\n- CAS-No.: 29435-48-1\n\n### 1.2 Relevant identified uses of the substance or mixture and uses advised against\n- Identified uses: Laboratory chemicals, Manufacture of substances\n\n### 1.3 Details of the supplier of the safety data sheet\n- Company: Sigma-Aldrich Chemie BV  \n  Stationsplein 4  \n  3331 LL ZWIJNDRECHT  \n  NETHERLANDS\n- Telephone: +31 78-620-5411\n- Fax: +31 78-620-5421\n- E-mail address: eurtechserv@sial.com\n\n### 1.4 Emergency telephone number\n- Emergency Phone #: 112\n\n## SECTION 2: Hazards identification\n\n### 2.1 Classification of the substance or mixture\nNot a hazardous substance or mixture according to Regulation (EC) No. 1272/2008.  \nThis substance is not classified as dangerous according to Directive 67/548/EEC.\n\n### 2.2 Label elements\nThe product does not need to be labelled in accordance with EC directives or respective national laws.\n\n### 2.3 Other hazards\n- none\n\n## SECTION 3: Composition/information on ingredients\n\n### 3.1 Substances\n- Synonyms: PHB  \n  (R)-3-Hydroxybutyric acid polymerized\n- CAS-No.: 29435-48-1\n\nNo components need to be disclosed according to the applicable regulations.\n\nAldrich - 363502  \nPage 1 of 6--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nArdacin (https://sitem.herts.ac.uk/aeru/vsdb/Reports/2569.htm)\nciteturn16search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month;  | Ardacin exhibits isomerism due to its nature as a glycopeptide antibiotic complex, composed of multiple structurally related components, Ardacin A, B, C, and C2.\n\nArdacin  | Image\nLast updated: 16/09/2025  | \n(Also known as: Aridicin)\n\nGENERAL INFORMATION ^{}\n | Image: General information\nDescription\n | Ardacin is a broad spectrum antibacterial glycopeptide with ruminal activity isolated from Kibdelosporangium aridum\nExamples of veterinary uses\n | Growth promoter. Reported uses inlude as a feedgrade antibiotic for enhancing digestive function and growth in grazing steers\nExamples of species treated\n | Cattle\nApproval status  | \nVMR 2013/2033 approval status (GB/UK)\n | Not approved\nEU Regulatory approval status\n | Not approved\nChemical structure  | ^{}\nIsomerism\n | Ardacin exhibits isomerism due to its nature as a glycopeptide antibiotic complex, composed of multiple structurally related components, Ardacin A, B, C, and C2. These variants arise from differences in the stereochemistry and substituent patterns on the glycopeptide backbone, which includes multiple chiral centres, aromatic rings, and sugar moieties.\nChemical formula\n | C₅₉H₄₇Cl₄N₇O₁₈\nCanonical SMILES\n | CCC(=O)NC1C(C(C(OC1O)C(=O)O)O)O.CNC1C2=CC(=C(C=C2)O)OC3=CC(=C(C(=C3)O)Cl)C4C(=O)NC5C6=CC(=C(C(=C6)OC7=C(C=C(C=C7Cl)C(C8C(=O)NC(C9=C(C(=CC(=C9)O)O)C2=C(C=CC(=C2)C(C(=O)N8)NC5=O)O)C(=O)O)O)Cl)O)OC2=C(C=C(C=C2)C(C(C(=O)N4)NC1=O)O)Cl\nIsomeric SMILES\n | CCC(=O)N[C@@H]1[C@H]([C@@H]([C@H](OC1O)C(=O)O)O)O.CNC1C2=CC(=C(C=C2)O)OC3=CC(=C(C(=C3)O)Cl)C4C(=O)NC5C6=CC(=C(C(=C6)OC7=C(C=C(C=C7Cl)C(C8C(=O)NC(C9=C(C(=CC(=C9)O)O)C2=C(C=CC(=C2)C(C(=O)N8)NC5=O)O)C(=O)O)O)Cl)O)OC2=C(C=C(C=C2)C(C(C(=O)N4)NC1=O)O)Cl\nInternational Chemical Identifier key (InChIKey)\n | ZHRODENVJFUAFN-PNKCYDOPSA-N\nInternational Chemical Identifier (InChI)\n | -\n2D structure diagram/image available?\n | Yes\nGeneral status  | ^{}\nVeterinary substance type\n | Antimicrobial, Antibacterial\nSubstance groups\n | Glycopeptide\nMinimum active substance purity\n | -\nKnown relevant impurities\n | -\nSubstance origin\n | -\nMode of action\n | Inhibition of muramyl-pentapeptide-acteylglucosamine transfer from the lipid carrier to the peptidoglaycan chain during cell wall synthesis\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPoly (R)-3-hydroxybutyric acid natural origin 29435-48-1 (https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/CL/en/product/aldrich/363502)\nciteturn16search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Sigma-Aldrich 363502 Poly[(R)-3-hydroxybutyric acid][Button: Quick View]  | Sigma-Aldrich 78239(R)-3-Phenylbutyric acid[Button: Quick View]\n\n363502\n\nImage: Poly[(R)-3-hydroxybutyric acid] natural origin\n\nImage: Poly[(R)-3-hydroxybutyric acid] natural origin\n\n### Key Documents\n\n  * COA\n\n  * COO\n\nView All Documentation\n\n363502\n\nImage: Sigma-Aldrich\n\nShare\n\n# Poly[(R)-3-hydroxybutyric acid]\n\n## natural origin\n\n(0)\n\n[Button: Write a review]\n\n[Button: Ask a question]\n\nSynonym(s):\n\n(R)-3-Hydroxybutyric acid polymerized, PHB\n\nSign In to View Organizational & Contract Pricing.\n\n### Select a Size\n\nChange View\n\nSize/SKU  | Availability  | Price\n--- | --- | ---\n10 g 363502-10G  | Check Cart for Availability  | CLP 206,000\n100 g 363502-100G  | Check Cart for Availability  | CLP 904,000\n\n* * *\n\n### About This Item\n\nLinear Formula:\n\n[COCH_{2}CH(CH_{3})O]_{n}\n\nCAS Number:\n\n29435-48-1\n\nNACRES:\n\nNA.23\n\nPubChem Substance ID:\n\n24862200\n\nUNSPSC Code:\n\n12162002\n\nMDL number:\n\nMFCD00134263\n\n## 363502-10G\n\n### CLP 206,000\n\n* * *\n\nCheck Cart for Availability\n\n* * *\n\n​\n\n[Input]\n\n[Button: Add to Cart]\n\nRequest a Custom Order\n\nTechnical Service\n\nNeed help? Our team of experienced scientists is here for you.\n\nLet Us Assist\n\nProperties\n\n### Quality Segment\n\n200\n\n### transition temp\n\nT_{m} 172 °C (DSC)\n\n### SMILES string\n\nCC(O)CC(O)=O\n\n### InChI\n\n1S/C12H20O6/c1-8(14)6-11(15)18-10(3)7-12(16)17-9(2)4-5-13/h5,8-10,14H,4,6-7H2,1-3H3\n\n### InChI key\n\nQLACRIKFZRFWRU-UHFFFAOYSA-N\n\nDescription\n\n### General description\n\nBiocompatible, biodegradable polymer.\n\n### Application\n\nPoly[(R)-3-hydroxybutyric acid (PHB) is a biodegradable and biocompatible polymer produced by several bacterial species, owing to its low resorbability and tunable properties, it may find uses in a variety of applications such as tissue engineering, controlled release systems etc.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAldrichimica Acta 40, 2007 (https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/deepweb/assets/sigmaaldrich/marketing/global/documents/220/677/acta-vol40.pdf)\nciteturn16search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.4 years ago; has led to innovative products that have found their way into Sigma-Aldrich’s catalogs. ... 363502\nPoly[(R)-3-hydroxybutyric acid]\nProfessor Seebach’s remarkable creativeness in chemical synthesis \nhas led to innovative products that have found their way into Sigma-Aldrich’s catalogs.\nBelow is a selection of products that are strongly associated \nwith his outstanding contributions to organic chemistry.\nPHB\nBrand\nProd. No.\nName\nAldrich\n298360\n(R)-(–)-3-Hydroxybutyric acid sodium \nsalt\nAldrich\n363502\nPoly[(R)-3-hydroxybutyric acid]\nBrand Aldrich 157872 1,3-Dithiane | Prod. No. None | Name None --- | --- | --- Brand Aldrich 359130 2-Methyl-1,3-dithiane | Prod. No. None | Name None Brand Aldrich 220817 2-(Trimethylsilyl)-1,3-dithiane | Prod. No. None | Name None Brand Aldrich 282138 Bis(trimethylsilyl)methane | Prod. No. None | Name None Brand Aldrich 226335 B